+/*
+ * Wait out the firmware's answer to a descriptor publication.
+ *
+ * A descriptor the MIPS has not seen before is a VideoDec signal event: it runs
+ * HandleSignalEvent/WCE and programs the source-0 geometry, stride and mode
+ * registers from the record itself (doku/76 11.3, measured 06.09.2026). Almost
+ * everything it computes there is what this driver writes anyway -- geometry
+ * 0x043f077f/0x00420077, crop 0x04380780/0x021c0780, luma stride 0x780 -- with
+ * one exception: the record carries a single stride, so the WCE puts the luma
+ * pitch into the chroma stride as well and undoes the NV16 doubling that is the
+ * point of this plane. That is the whole of the cold-start bug: the plane came
+ * up with a halved chroma stride and every other register correct, out of
+ * exactly the two prior states in which the pointer was not already standing --
+ * a cold start, and a run after the bring-up script had cleared it
+ * (doku/nachtlog/D-cstride-befund.md).
+ *
+ * The event is asynchronous and the ARM side has no completion signal for it,
+ * so it is bracketed instead: the caller parks a value in the chroma stride
+ * that the WCE cannot produce -- zero is not a legal stride -- and this waits
+ * for the WCE to replace it. That is also the proven ordering: the bring-up
+ * recipe publishes the descriptor and configures source 0 as two separate
+ * steps, and its chroma stride has always stuck (doku/78 A, stage 7a before
+ * 7b).
+ *
+ * Source 0 is not selected downstream while this runs and the caller programs
+ * the register for real afterwards, so the parked value never reaches the
+ * panel.
+ *
+ * The budget is the only bound the board has given and nothing narrower. On
+ * the cold start of 07.09.2026 the descriptor write, the firmware's answer and
+ * the driver's source-0 programming all fell into a single 1 s sampling
+ * interval (doku/nachtlog/D-abnahme-board.md, the 06:15 table), so "inside one
+ * second" is the whole of what has been measured. A 60 Hz capture loop makes
+ * ~17 ms the expected latency, but expecting is not measuring, and a budget
+ * shorter than the measured bound would end the wait while the firmware is
+ * still entitled to answer -- and then produce exactly the halved chroma
+ * stride this bracket exists to prevent. It costs at most one wait per boot,
+ * because the caller only gets here when the publication was new. Narrowing it
+ * needs the measurement in doku/nachtlog/D-cstride-fix.md section 4 C.
+ *
+ * Return: 0 once the firmware has replaced the marker, -ETIMEDOUT if it has
+ * not by the deadline. What that means is the caller's to say, because only
+ * the caller knows what it is about to program.
+ */
+static int h713_afbd_wait_wce(struct h713_afbd *h)
+{
+	u32 c_stride;
+
+	return readl_poll_timeout(h->regs + AFBD_VIDEO_C_STRIDE, c_stride,
+				  c_stride, 100, H713_WCE_TIMEOUT_US);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Publish the descriptor and hand the firmware the pointer to it -- ONCE per
+ * boot, and never withdraw it.
+ *
+ * Every change to this record is a signal event to the firmware: it re-runs
+ * HandleSignalEvent/WCE and reprograms stride and mode registers behind the
+ * driver's back. Doing that a second time froze the picture and left the
+ * capture wedged until the next cold start (doku/76 11.3); why it does not
+ * recover is open (RE question K3). The content comparison below makes this
+ * idempotent even across a module reload, because the reserved page keeps the
+ * record across one.
+ *
